{
  "title": "iOS UI tests: app main thread stalls minutes when the simulator suspends the InputUI keyboard process",
  "description": "In run 37389551049 (PR #762), testLoginFailure failed with 'Failed to get matching snapshot: Unable to perform work on main run loop, process main thread busy for 30.0s'. \
The test typed the server URL, then tapped the Username field at about 23:49:53 UTC. \
The app's main thread then stayed blocked until about 23:54:05. \
The simulator system log in that run's ios-ui-test-results artifact shows the cause: InputUI (the out-of-process keyboard, pid 15888) was launched fresh at 23:49:45 on the first keyboard use of the run. \
At 23:49:51.7 runningboardd sent it 'process assertions expiration warning' and then suspended it (SpringBoard: 'osservice<com.apple.InputUI>, running-suspended-NotVisible' at 23:50:07), even though the keyboard was on screen. \
Meanwhile the app's main thread logged '-[UIKeyboardTaskQueue _lockWhenReadyForMainThread] Keyboard queue task timeout detected' at 23:49:53, 23:50:03 and 23:52:49, and logged almost nothing else between 23:50:03 and 23:52:48. \
InputUI logged nothing from 23:50:02 until a brief assertion woke it at 23:53:21, and it only became fully active around 23:54:03, when the app recovered. \
Runner 1-minute load was about 188 when InputUI was suspended, then fell to about 9 while the app stayed blocked. \
So the stall itself is not CPU starvation, though the load may explain why the assertion lapsed. \
Ideas, none tried yet: warm up the keyboard in scripts/prepare-ios-ui-simulator.sh configure, so InputUI is not cold-launched mid-test; connect the simulator hardware keyboard so the tests don't drive the software keyboard through InputUI; check whether this reproduces locally on an iOS 26.5 simulator. \
Related, but a different symptom: issues/p3-ios-ui-app-launch-hang.json5.",
  "status": "open",
